<title>UK: Korea Data sets 22 mln Sfr convertible.</title>
<headline>Korea Data sets 22 mln Sfr convertible.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Data Systems has issued a 22 million Swiss franc five-year convertible bond, lead manager Credit Suisse said.</p>
<p>The bond pays 1/8 percent coupon and is priced at par. The issue is puttable on November 28, 1999 at 111.42, giving a yield to put of 3.79 percent.</p>
<p>It is callable from 1998 subject to a 130 percent hurdle.</p>
<p>Conversion price is 133,427 won, a premium of 15 percent.</p>
<p>The conversion period is between December 19, 96 and October 27, 2001. Forex rate is 1,656.25 won per Swiss franc.</p>
<p>Maturity date is November 28, 2001. Payment date is November 28, 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
